    <bf:title>
      <bf:Title>
	<bf:mainTitle>A military history of the Levant during the era of the Crusades</bf:mainTitle>
	<bflc:nonSortNum>2</bflc:nonSortNum>
      </bf:Title>
    </bf:title>
    <bf:content>
      <bf:Content rdf:about="http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/contentTypes/txt">
	<rdfs:label>text</rdfs:label>
	<bf:code>txt</bf:code>
      </bf:Content>
    </bf:content>
    <bf:supplementaryContent>
      <bf:SupplementaryContent rdf:about="http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/msupplcont/bibliography">
	<rdfs:label>bibliography</rdfs:label>
	<bf:code>bibliography</bf:code>
      </bf:SupplementaryContent>
    </bf:supplementaryContent>
    <bf:summary>
      <bf:Summary>
	<rdfs:label>"Each chapter is written from the viewpoint of a different group. This approach gives voice to various groups, including crusaders, local Latin princes and neighbouring Muslim powers, providing the readers with a deeper understanding of the crusades. Featuring contributions from leading scholars, this book combines narrative and analysis to deliver fresh insights into the era's military dynamics"-- Provided by publisher.</rdfs:label>
      </bf:Summary>
    </bf:summary>
    <bf:tableOfContents>
      <bf:TableOfContents>
	<rdfs:label>Volume 1. Twelfth century. First Crusade / John France -- County of Edessa / Alan V. Murray -- Principality of Antioch / Andrew D. Buck -- Kingdom of Jerusalem / Steve Tibble -- County of Tripoli / Kevin James Lewis -- Second Crusade / Jason Roche -- Seljuq Aleppo / James Wilson -- Burid Damascus / Alexander Mallett -- Zengids / Taef El-Azhari -- Shayzar under the Banu Munqidh / Niall Christie -- Nizari Ismaʿilis / Farhad Daftary -- Fatimid Egypt / Paul E. Walker -- Saladin / Yaacov Lev -- Third Crusade / Helen J. Nicholson -- Armenian Principalities / Federico Alpi.</rdfs:label>
      </bf:TableOfContents>
    </bf:tableOfContents>
    <bf:tableOfContents>
      <bf:TableOfContents>
	<rdfs:label>Volume 2. Thirteenth century. Kingdom of Jerusalem / Chris Marshall -- Antioch-Tripoli / Peter Edbury -- Lusignan Cyprus / Nicholas Coureas -- Fifth Crusade / Jessalynn Lea Bird -- Ayyubids / Bogdan C. Smarandache -- Crusade of Louis IX / M. Cecilia Gaposchkin -- Mongols / Timothy May -- Mamluks / Adam Ali -- Armenian Kingdoms / Federico Alpi.</rdfs:label>
      </bf:TableOfContents>
    </bf:tableOfContents>
